  "worked_solution": "he third equation states that  $z=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+2(\\frac{1}{2})=2\\,\u27f9\\,y=2-1=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $y=1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx-(1)-(\\frac{1}{2})=4\\,\u27f9\\,x=4+1+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{11}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{11}{2}$,  $y=1$, and $z=\\frac{1}{2}.$  In vector form, the solution can be written as $\u27e8\\frac{11}{2},1,\\frac{1}{2}\u27e9.$",
